// tests/fixtures/err_interpolation_hole_undefined_name.ubl
// A second, real, pre-existing gap this delivery fixed alongside format
// specs: interpolation holes were PARSED (a broken hole was always a
// real parse error) but never actually name-resolved or type-checked --
// `resolve_expr`'s `ExprKind::Lit(_) => {}` arm matched
// `InterpolatedStr` too, so nothing inside a `{expr}` hole was ever
// walked by name resolution at all. Invisible at runtime (the
// interpreter resolves identifiers by name, independent of sema's
// resolution map -- see interpreter/eval/expr.rs), but a real, silent
// gap in static checking: this exact program used to sema-pass cleanly.
// Expected: sema FAIL (UndefinedName).

fn main() void {
    println($"this references nothing real: {does_not_exist}")
}
